        4
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Beacon_Hill%2C_Boston"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The neighborhood’s first community council formed in 1922 to stop new construction and protect its historic brick sidewalks.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6,
        7
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Beacon_Hill%2C_Boston"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Before European settlement, Beacon Hill was part of the traditional lands of the Duwamish people.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.beaconhillcouncilseattle.org/our-history"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Beacon Hill’s historic district was declared a National Historic Landmark on December 19, 1962.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Beacon_Hill%2C_Boston"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "The neighborhood’s brick sidewalks survived a 1940s city plan to replace them thanks to strong community opposition.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
